{#
  The home addresses the crowdsec-home-ips CronJob looks up, and the crowdsec-jobs sidecar's
  home allowlist reads (files/home_ips_discover.py, files/home_allowlist.py).

  DECIDED: rendered with no `data` keys, so each field has one writer. The object must exist
  before the first run, because RBAC cannot narrow `create` by name and the CronJob's Role
  grants `patch` on this one name only. With no `data` in the render, Ansible's client-side
  apply records none in its last-applied annotation, and a later Flux server-side apply owns
  none, so neither removes or reverts a field the CronJob wrote. The operator accepted the same
  field-ownership argument for deploy/ghcr-mirror on #5732.
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ crowdsec_k8s_home_ips_configmap }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
